## What was measured
Source: `results/quality/pass2.json` and `pass2.txt`, run as pre-registered in `docs/photo_quality_check.md`, on the disease validation ({{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.n}} images) and test ({{results/quality/pass2.json::test.n}} images) sets. Degradations are synthetic and are not real phone failures.

| | Validation | Test |
|---|---|---|
| Originals rejected | {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.originals_rejected}} of {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.n}} | {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.originals_rejected}} of {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.n}} |
| Darkened to 20% flagged too dark | {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.caught_for_expected_reason.darkened to 20%}} of {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.n}} | {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.caught_for_expected_reason.darkened to 20%}} of {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.n}} |
| Glare +150 flagged too bright | {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.caught_for_expected_reason.glare +150}} of {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.n}} | {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.caught_for_expected_reason.glare +150}} of {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.n}} |

The rejected originals were rejected for being under the minimum side (validation {{results/quality/pass2.json::validation.by_issue.too_small}}, test {{results/quality/pass2.json::test.by_issue.too_small}}) or, before the blur check was switched off, for blur. No original was rejected for darkness or brightness. The glare degradation (adding 150 to every pixel) is not a physical glare model, so the 77 to 80% figure shows only how the brightness limit reacts to it.

## The blur check and why it is off
The blur limit (variance of the Laplacian below 30) was tested against criteria fixed beforehand and failed them on the validation split: it rejected {{results/quality/pass2.json::blur_decision.originals_rejected_for_blur::.4f}} of sharp originals, against a limit of 0.02 (it caught {{results/quality/pass2.json::blur_decision.radius4_flagged_blurry::.4f}} of radius-4 copies, which met its criterion). The check is therefore switched off, and sharpness is reported as not reliably measurable on this data. This was a near miss, not a clear failure. A first calibration pass using percentile limits was rejected earlier (`results/quality/calibration.txt`). Laplacian variance depends on resolution and content, and none of this transfers to phone photos.

## Limitations
- Studio-style images only. No phone photo was available, so the module has never been tried on real photos.
- Does not check sharpness or framing. A blurry or badly framed maize leaf can pass.
- A leaf that fills the frame cannot be measured by a green-pixel share without rejecting yellow, nutrient-deficient leaves, so no such check exists.
- The test split was used twice for quality reports. No model is tuned on it.
- A blurry or dark photo tends to produce low-confidence model results, which fusion treats as not assessed. This was not measured.